      "data": {
        "official_name": "CVE JSON Record Format",
        "common_name": null,
        "alternate_names": ["CVE JSON Schema", "CVE Record Format"],
        "description": "JSON schema defining the structure of CVE records, maintained by the CVE Project. Used by CVE Services API, cvelistV5 repository, and all CNAs submitting CVE records.",
        "notes": "The 5.x schema accepts any 5.x record — the dataVersion pattern is ^5\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)(\\....)$. Older 5.0 and 5.1 records remain valid against the latest 5.x schema. Legacy pre-5.0 formats (1.0–4.0) are archived under schema/archive/ in CVEProject/cve-schema: 4.0 provides three state-specific JSON Schemas (public, reject, reserved) with strong markers (data_type: \"CVE\", data_format: \"MITRE\", data_version: \"4.0\"); 3.1 provides a JSON Schema whose only marker is data_version (string); 1.0 and 2.0 have Markdown specifications only (no JSON Schema — recognise only).\n\nNote on versioning: version_required is false because the schema version IS the subpath identifier (e.g., #5.2.0). There are no items within a version — each version is a leaf. The version_required pattern is for sources where versions wrap a hierarchy of items (e.g., OWASP Top 10 2021 → A01-A10).",
        "version_required": false,
        "versions_available": [
